        "department": null,
        "description": "With advent of different computing platform, e.g., mobile phones, smart-watches, smart-TVs, VR, Web, we are surrounded by interactive systems and we use them regularly for pleasure, accessing service, or even by compulsion. Despite tremendous progress in technology, many of the current day systems are hard to use for a non-tech savvy population? The course will teach you how to design and develop usable interactive systems. It will also develop skills to analyze and critique existing systems and understand ways by which some of these systems may be violating some of the fundamental usability principles and what can be done to fix it.",
